## At work

- your employer can make sure there are gluten free options at work events and canteens
- a place to store and heat your own food helps
- you may need time off for appointments and scans

## Is coeliac disease a disability?

Under the **Equality Act 2010**, a condition counts as a disability if it has a **substantial** (more than minor) and **long-term** (12 months or more) effect on your normal daily activities. The law looks at how you would be **without treatment**. Some people with coeliac disease may be covered, especially if they have other related conditions. Each case is different.

## Benefits

Coeliac disease on its own does not usually qualify for disability benefits such as PIP.

## Costs

Gluten free food often costs more. Some areas provide gluten free bread and flour mixes on prescription. Prescriptions are **free in Wales**. In England, check if you can get free prescriptions with our [NHS health costs check](/support/health-costs/checker/).
